{"uid":"4efb3496bf7521e3","name":"test_pre_dispatch_record_run_dir_still_renders","fullName":"tests.test_browser_hub#test_pre_dispatch_record_run_dir_still_renders","historyId":"f75997e1f4d80be57fb8372e77aada0a","time":{"start":1791895031514,"stop":1791895037988,"duration":6474},"description":"Task 038 (G.6): a run dir written BEFORE the dispatch-record change\n    (task 027, F.1's `assignedTaskId`/`effectiveTier` on each iteration's own\n    `meta.json`, and task 030, F.4's `engineVersion` on `status.json`) must\n    still render -- as blank or an em dash where those fields would have\n    gone -- rather than raising anywhere along the chain (`engine.state.\n    iteration_detail`/`task_totals`, `ui_server.run_detail`, `app.js`'s\n    `renderTimeline`/`renderTasks`/`renderSummary`).\n\n    The fixture is exactly that pre-change shape: `_base_meta()` with none\n    of its `over` kwargs used, so the written `meta.json` carries no\n    `assignedTaskId`/`effectiveTier` key at all (not merely a null value --\n    absent, the way a real pre-027 iteration dir would be), and\n    `_write_dead_run`'s default `status.json` (no `engineVersion` kwarg),\n    the same default `test_run_page_shows_the_engine_version_it_is_executing`\n    (task 035) opts OUT of by passing `engineVersion=\"0.21.0\"` explicitly --\n    here it is left out on purpose.\n    ","descriptionHtml":"<p>Task 038 (G.6): a run dir written BEFORE the dispatch-record change<br />\n(task 027, F.1's <code>assignedTaskId</code>/<code>effectiveTier</code> on each iteration's own<br />\n<code>meta.json</code>, and task 030, F.4's <code>engineVersion</code> on <code>status.json</code>) must<br />\nstill render -- as blank or an em dash where those fields would have<br />\ngone -- rather than raising anywhere along the chain (<code>engine.state. iteration_detail</code>/<code>task_totals</code>, <code>ui_server.run_detail</code>, <code>app.js</code>'s<br />\n<code>renderTimeline</code>/<code>renderTasks</code>/<code>ren